# MTG Search Repo Architecture

## Monorepo layout
- `api/`: FastAPI backend + worker + tests (Python 3.12, uv-managed)
- `frontend/`: React + TypeScript + Vite app
- `.github/workflows/`: CI workflows
- Root `README.md`: operational runbook and deployment overview

## Backend structure (`api/src/oracle_tutor_api/`)
- `api/`: HTTP endpoints and search API composition
- `worker/`: one-shot ingestion/update jobs and data pipelines
- `core/`: shared config, DB, models, logging, initialization
- Keep transport concerns in `api/`, ingestion concerns in `worker/`, shared infra/domain helpers in `core/`.

## Frontend structure (`frontend/src/`)
- `components/`: reusable UI components
- `pages/`: route-level page views
- `lib/`: UI/shared helpers
- `api.ts`: backend API integration point
- Prefer page orchestration in `pages/`, reusable view logic in `components/`, pure helpers in `lib/`.

## Architectural guardrails
- Avoid backend-worker circular coupling except through explicit shared `core` utilities.
- Avoid frontend components calling arbitrary fetch logic directly when a shared API module already exists.
- Keep deployment/runtime concerns in Docker/nginx/workflow files, not business logic modules.
